[{:db/id 17592186087840 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5fbef9b7-68b9-5b6d-beff-b38a63574b1c"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5fbef9b7-68b9-5b6d-beff-b38a63574b1c" :question/id #uuid "5fbef9b7-68b9-5b6d-beff-b38a63574b1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-16458" :question/problem "![](images/2a/2adb84964a605495c84921943ec76f9820ba18851cda817037dd6022808d1fd7.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-29540716-87b2-5957-a8c4-7141164fdefb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-29540716-87b2-5957-a8c4-7141164fdefb" :answer-field/id #uuid "29540716-87b2-5957-a8c4-7141164fdefb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9428f7fa-4636-5ad9-ac5c-92e2a7fbe6ab" :answer-field/choices ["answer-64c8fe0e-8e01-5ebd-869d-3e05d36b78cb" "answer-239820f5-492c-5074-bb16-a6af5ed54f89" "answer-224b79cf-bf9d-546e-92e5-652da96853b2" "answer-9428f7fa-4636-5ad9-ac5c-92e2a7fbe6ab" "answer-53b5a01d-de71-5112-abcb-3f57176855d3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-64c8fe0e-8e01-5ebd-869d-3e05d36b78cb" :answer/id #uuid "64c8fe0e-8e01-5ebd-869d-3e05d36b78cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-239820f5-492c-5074-bb16-a6af5ed54f89" :answer/id #uuid "239820f5-492c-5074-bb16-a6af5ed54f89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-224b79cf-bf9d-546e-92e5-652da96853b2" :answer/id #uuid "224b79cf-bf9d-546e-92e5-652da96853b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9428f7fa-4636-5ad9-ac5c-92e2a7fbe6ab" :answer/id #uuid "9428f7fa-4636-5ad9-ac5c-92e2a7fbe6ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-53b5a01d-de71-5112-abcb-3f57176855d3" :answer/id #uuid "53b5a01d-de71-5112-abcb-3f57176855d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087841 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-cb8398f9-e97a-58eb-bd8b-b49ccd2d689d" "question-3c46acbe-8af8-5805-a582-9ade9300c9a5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-cb8398f9-e97a-58eb-bd8b-b49ccd2d689d" :question/id #uuid "cb8398f9-e97a-58eb-bd8b-b49ccd2d689d" :question/math-academy-id "q-279167" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=49$ and ${b}^{2}=25.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=49,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=25,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=5.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 5=10.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-878be2a7-5abd-5dc4-9fe0-30ce370e3435" "answer-field-13f8d6b7-9861-51ad-96d2-5cd3b96789b2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-878be2a7-5abd-5dc4-9fe0-30ce370e3435" :answer-field/id #uuid "878be2a7-5abd-5dc4-9fe0-30ce370e3435" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-56513915-f193-5d63-936d-07a8b133ceae" :answer-field/choices ["answer-56513915-f193-5d63-936d-07a8b133ceae"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-56513915-f193-5d63-936d-07a8b133ceae" :answer/id #uuid "56513915-f193-5d63-936d-07a8b133ceae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-13f8d6b7-9861-51ad-96d2-5cd3b96789b2" :answer-field/id #uuid "13f8d6b7-9861-51ad-96d2-5cd3b96789b2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-bb06d992-e82f-5977-a714-2f2fd87616b9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bb06d992-e82f-5977-a714-2f2fd87616b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb06d992-e82f-5977-a714-2f2fd87616b9" :answer/id #uuid "bb06d992-e82f-5977-a714-2f2fd87616b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3c46acbe-8af8-5805-a582-9ade9300c9a5" :question/id #uuid "3c46acbe-8af8-5805-a582-9ade9300c9a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-279199" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{13}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=13$ and ${b}^{2}=36.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=13,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{13}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=36,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=6,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{13}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 6=12,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{13}=2\\sqrt{13}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5f59ee40-6a49-5f76-9b09-b56f1e7b8c65" "answer-field-62dc0b83-a470-59d2-b62b-b5ccbaa907c1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5f59ee40-6a49-5f76-9b09-b56f1e7b8c65" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f59ee40-6a49-5f76-9b09-b56f1e7b8c65" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-1dcd62ed-d1d5-5d66-b9a7-d3752b72ffcb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1dcd62ed-d1d5-5d66-b9a7-d3752b72ffcb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1dcd62ed-d1d5-5d66-b9a7-d3752b72ffcb" :answer/id #uuid "1dcd62ed-d1d5-5d66-b9a7-d3752b72ffcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-62dc0b83-a470-59d2-b62b-b5ccbaa907c1" :answer-field/id #uuid "62dc0b83-a470-59d2-b62b-b5ccbaa907c1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-2cb3f03d-cfef-5f9f-b396-26b221d4f856" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2cb3f03d-cfef-5f9f-b396-26b221d4f856"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cb3f03d-cfef-5f9f-b396-26b221d4f856" :answer/id #uuid "2cb3f03d-cfef-5f9f-b396-26b221d4f856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-2d86a4f4-b8ba-5875-b01b-334ee3c8800c" :activity/id #uuid "2d86a4f4-b8ba